WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.720
Most people who pay close attention to pop
culture are aware of Donald Glover's extreme

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.880
range of talents.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.800
He's the Emmy-winning creator, writer, star,
and occasional director of the FX series Atlanta,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.580
the Grammy-winning rapper Childish Gambino,
and even the young version of Lando Calrissian.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.840
But before Glover was all of those things
and more, he was shining bright as the lovable

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.840
jock Troy Barnes on the beloved sitcom Community.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.160
"You'd be surprised at how many of your favorite
football players got started at community

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:27.660
college.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.140
“Really, name one.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.580
Who's your favorite player?”

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.580
“Me, whoa."

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.219
Running for six seasons between 2009 and 2015,
Community focused on the bizarre and whimsical

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.620
exploits of a group of seven students attending
a community college.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.160
It was never a huge hit in the ratings, but
it had a devoted fanbase and helped kickstart

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.060
the careers of its cast members.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.460
Sadly, during the hiatus in 2013 between Community's
fourth and fifth seasons, it was announced

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.800
that Glover would be leaving the show at some
point during the upcoming season.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:02.040
NBC wound up cancelling Community after season
5, and though the now-defunct streaming service

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:02.540
Yahoo!

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.220
Screen revived it for a sixth season, it never
fully recovered its early magic without Glover

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:07.880
around anymore.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.240
So why did he leave in the first place?

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.240
Let's investigate.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:17.240
In 2011, during Community's third season,
NBC put the show on an indefinite hiatus.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.400
While it did return later that season, it
was an ominous sign of what was to come.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.560
In May 2012, after the third season ended,
Sony Television, which produced the show,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.040
fired creator Dan Harmon.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:33.070
Then after a rocky season 4, regular cast
member Chevy Chase left the show as well,

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:37.320
in the wake of his increasingly aggressive
and reportedly racist on-set behavior.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.760
Considering all this turmoil, it's not all
that surprising that Glover decided to take

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:46.310
the star power he gained from Community and
try something new on a show that was decidedly

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:47.920
calmer behind the scenes.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.020
In August 2013, it was announced that Glover
was creating the half-hour comedy-drama Atlanta

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:53.820
for FX.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.700
Though Harmon eventually returned for Community's
fifth season and even managed to persuade

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.039
Glover to appear on five episodes before truly
calling it quits, he admitted that Glover

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.520
had outgrown the series.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.850
A few months after Glover announced his impending
departure from Community, he revealed that

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.800
his reasons for leaving were more than just
professional in nature.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.880
In October 2013, he posted to Instagram a
series of letters explaining that he left

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:20.870
Community because he wanted to be on his own
and was working through difficult events in

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.300
his personal life that made him reassess what
he truly wanted to do.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.850
He admitted to a ton of fears, including that
he was worried that Dan Harmon hated him,

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.930
that he was scared of "letting everyone down"
by moving on from Community, and that he believed

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.660
his future projects might fail.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.260
That kind of stress adds up.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:45.420
“ahh.”

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.280
Nevertheless, he said that he wanted to release
his album Because the Internet that Christmas

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.080
to give people hope for the next year.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.660
Shortly thereafter, Glover clarified his jumbled
thoughts in an interview with VIBE, noting

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.100
that his heart really wasn't in it anymore
and while Community was a great show, it wasn't

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:01.700
his show.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.960
“I just want to make dope,dope s--- from
now on, like on my own terms."

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.360
In 2016, Glover was more direct about his
decision to depart from Community.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.400
Two years after his last episode aired and
a year after the show wrapped for good, he

00:03:15.401 --> 00:03:19.390
revealed that he chose to leave partially
because he appreciates the future opportunities

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.740
that endings create.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.020
At the Television Critics Association summer
tour, Glover explained that while he wasn't

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.910
trying to run away from Community, he feels
that every good thing must come to an end

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.450
in order for growth to happen.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.920
This, of course, includes his run on the sitcom.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:33.920
As he explained,

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.340
"I just like endings.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.400
I think everything should have death clauses
in them like humans have death clauses [...] It's

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.730
important that things end.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.340
It forces events to progress."

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:47.520
Since leaving Community, Glover has received
seven Emmy nominations, including two wins,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.480
and seven Grammy nominations, including five
wins.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.340
As for Glover's fears about his Community
colleagues' resenting him for leaving them

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.820
behind, they appear to have nothing but love
and admiration for him.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.300
Troy's sailing endeavor may not have gone
well, but Glover's horizon is burning bright.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.820
"Now, Troy, I know it's gonna be difficult
for you to interact with me."

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.320
"No, no.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.560
That was the original Troy.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.400
I'm his clone.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.220
Let's get the lead out, Burton."

